          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Years in Politics</strong><br>\nHelmut Kohl began his political career as a member of the Christian Democratic Union (CDU), rapidly rising through its ranks to become the youngest chairman of a German federal state, Rhineland-Palatinate.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Road to Chancellorship</strong><br>\nIn 1976, Kohl was nominated as the CDU's candidate for chancellor, but it wasn't until 1982 that he assumed the office, following a constructive vote of no confidence against Chancellor Helmut Schmidt.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Economic Policies and Reforms</strong><br>\nKohl's tenure was marked by efforts to revitalize the German economy through market-oriented reforms. His government implemented several measures to reduce state intervention and promote private enterprise.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>German Reunification</strong><br>\nKohl's most significant achievement was his decisive role in the reunification of East and West Germany. He is often called the \"Chancellor of Unity\" for his leadership during this historic period.</p>\n\n<p><strong>European Integration</strong><br>\nKohl was a committed Europeanist, pushing for further integration of the continent. He played a key role in the creation of the Euro and the expansion of the European Union.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Challenges</strong><br>\nKohl's later years as chancellor were challenged by economic stagnation and high unemployment. Nevertheless, he remained in office until 1998, making him the longest-serving chancellor of post-war Germany.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
